Z||000000||KRMFiero||10-22-2000||08:56 PM||||I currently own a 1984 Fiero 2M4 SE and This winter I am going to remove the engine and get it done .020 Over and some other preformance componates put on...  any suggestions??<P><BR>But I have wanted to do a V-8 conversion or a 3800... someone told me my 84 Automatic is the hardest to do the conversion in? So what year should I looke for if i want to do this? Auto or Stick?    I have been looking in Junk Yards and stuff for Fiero's needing Engines and I have found a couple but they are mainly Tech 4's <p>[This message has been edited by KRMFiero (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-22-2000||09:53 PM||||The 84 was designed with the 4 cylinder engine in mind, so the wiring in front of the engine is a pain for rewireing.<P>The 85-88 the wiring had the 2.8 as an option so all the wiring in front of the engine is there. Even the 4 cylinder engine has the right wires.<P>The 88 has a better suspension, but due to limited production, not much available for replacement parts.<P>Transmission choice is yours.  Manual transmissions are fun if you don't mind shifting.  Automatics are nice if you're driving in traffic.<P>Some 84 engines had some "weak" rods which blew through the engine when they broke. (Cause of fires)  If you have a 16 year old car and they haven't let loose you probably have a good engine or the engine has been replaced.<P>If you do the swap yourself, $2000. If you farm it out $5000.<P>Phil is from RI, he has a 3800 s/c with a manual transmission and he loves his yellow coupe. ||||reg||11
Z||000002||Phil||10-22-2000||10:54 PM||||That's stealth yellow. 38000 mi since Aug 99 and no probs yet( I drive it a lot).||||reg||1
